      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "<p>We the witnesses who have signed below were in the presence of Maim\u016bn b. Khalfah al-Magh[reb\u012b], known as Ibn al-Yat\u012bm, at a time that he was sick. We therefore inquired of him concerning what other people owed him and what he owed others, in connection with his being sick in a strange country\u2014for perhaps, goodness forbid, death might come to him, and then everything which others owed him and everything which he owed others would be lost. So he dictated his assets and liabilities to us, each and every thing, we marking it down word for word. Now the afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn rema[rked] that, belonging to the elder Ab\u016b\u2019l-Fa\u1e0dl Sahl b. Yefet b. Solomon, known as Ibn al-Sukkar\u012b, in his [Maim\u016bn\u2019s] keeping, was that which he had brought in the boat belonging to the elder Ab\u016b\u2019l-Sur\u016br Fara\u1e25 b. \u2018A\u1e6d\u012byyah, his end be good!\u2014namely, a bale of cotton, a wicker-work crate of copper on top of it, a mattress fastened upon it, a wicker-work crate of books, Iraqian copper containers filled with copper, on all of which was inscribed \u201c\u1e25\u0113n w\u0101\u1e25esed\u201d in reddish-brown ink; a bundle of coarse cloth on which was inscribed \u201cMaim\u016bn b. al-Yat\u012bm\u201d\u2014the afore-mentioned remarked that in it were a gold bracelet, eighteen small pieces of silver, jar-lids, signet rings and broken iron rings. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked also that, belonging to the elder Ab\u016b\u2019l-Khair Faraj b. Nahum, was a bundle of carpeting, a canvass-covered basket, a cage of glass, and a small wicker-work crate of copper. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked that, belonging to the elder Ab\u016b Ya\u1e25y\u0101 Naharai, were three boxes of books and a small sack in which were books; the afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked that he had taken them from the house of the elder Ab\u016b\u2019l-Bishr Azhar b. Ibr\u0101him at the instance of the afore-mentioned R. Naharai and his written command; also in the sack were three copies of the Torah and Prophets belonging to \u1e24asan b. Kulaib al-\u2018Askal\u0101n\u012b. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked also that he had taken along a basket on which was inscribed \u201cMaim\u016bn,\u201d but Maim\u016bn had nothing in it. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn also remarked that he had acquired a crystal vase which he had purchased for four dinars less a fourth of a dinar, half of the value of which was the afore-mentioned Ya\u2019ir\u2019s while half of the value was the afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn\u2019s; Maim\u016bn mentioned that he had sent it to the West, to Manasseh b. M\u016bs\u0101 in order that he should sell it, and whatever God decreed [as the price] would be equally divided between them. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked that belonging to the afore-mentioned Ya\u2019ir b. Abraham in his keeping was one dinar. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn acknowledged that he had with him nothing except three dinars and a half, the total. He also remarked that he had given to M\u016bs\u0101 b. M\u016bs\u0101 b. Maj\u0101n a wicker-work crate in which were ten mann of sal ammoniac for Ab\u016b\u2019l-Faraj b. El\u2018azar al-Maghreb\u012b, in order that he should give it over to him. The afore-mentioned Maim\u016bn remarked that belonging to him in the keeping of the afore-mentioned M\u016bs\u0101 b. Maj\u0101n were three dinars and one-sixth, from the value of . . . cotton and miscellaneous goods, all of which is in partnership between them. And that which transpired before us we have written and signed to, that it may serve after this day for a legal instrument and a proof: on Thursday, which is the seventeenth day in the month of Tammuz of the year one thousand three hundred and eighty-three according to the era to which we are accustomed here in Fus\u1e6d\u0101\u1e6d-Mi\u1e63r, which is situated on the Nile River, certified and established! Suspended between the lines is [the phrase] \u201cthat he\u201d and it is [thus] established, and its establishment is legally valid.</p>\n<p>Joseph b. El\u2018azar ha-Shofet</p>\n<p>Moses b. Solomon</p>",
